        {
          "text": "**Examining source decisions**\n\nI think it’s not essential to include the Human Rights Campaign (HRC) in my discussion, but it could be supportive of the Equality Act. However, since we already have direct vote sources, I can reduce reliance on Axios articles for context and focus on primary sources.\n\nThe load-bearing statements I want to present include: \n\n1) Jeffries voted Yea on the Equality Act, citing Clerk and VoteSmart for specifics on his vote. \n2) He also voted Yea on the Emmett Till Anti-Lynching Act, with references from VoteSmart. \n3) Finally, he voted Yea on the UFLPA.",
